ns\n\nReproducible in: 4.5.1.stable (Steam)\nUntested in any further version\n\n### System information\n\nGodot v4.5.1.stable (f62fdbde1) - Windows 11 (build 26200) - Multi-window, 3 monitors - Vulkan (Forward+) - dedicated NVIDIA GeForce RTX 3070 (NVIDIA; 32.0.15.8129) - 13th Gen Intel(R) Core(TM) i5-13600KF (20 threads) - 63.81 GiB memory\n\n### Issue description\n\nPopupMenu (as a child of OptionButton) doesn't inherit the Default Texture Filter from both its parent and the project itself.\n\nIf the project and the parent of the PopupMenu are set to Nearest Filtering, the PopupMenu will remain the new project default of Linear Filtering.\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n- Set rendering/textures/canvas_textures/default_texture_filter to Nearest.\n- Create a new theme and set the PopupMenu.panel property to a StyleBoxTexture.\n- Assign an AtlasTexture to that StyleBoxTexture.\n- Use a pixel art UI texture inside the AtlasTexture, then configure its region and texture margins.\n- Create a new scene with a Control node as the root.\n- Add an OptionButton to the scene and add several items to it.\n- Apply the theme you created to the OptionButton.\n- Set the OptionButton's texture_filter to Nearest.\n- Run the project and click the OptionButton.\n\nResult:\nThe PopupMenu appears blurry, while any pixel art texture directly assigned to the OptionButton itself renders correctly with nearest filtering.\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\n[bug_report2.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/24090593/bug_report2.zip)\n\nThis doesn't seem to be project-dependent, but we'll see.","closed_by":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/following{/other_user}"